{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"7f3bc3b9d8a678e0","type":"text","text":"Follow up paper on our LRU.","x":-29,"y":-17,"width":249,"height":77,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"c90498e35bece656","type":"text","text":"The realistic scenario in our paper is shallow, and it does not well represent real scenarios.","x":340,"y":-45,"width":260,"height":134,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ed7b82cbf23ef91e","type":"text","text":"Experimental realization of LRU.","x":741,"y":-141,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"addc52cc6e57da63","type":"text","text":"More detailed simulation.","x":741,"y":134,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"7fbb82e700bdda02","type":"text","text":"Simulate the 5-qubit code","x":1135,"y":133,"width":250,"height":58,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"cb1df84779d13aca","type":"text","text":"Experimental realization in quantum computers?","x":1135,"y":-143,"width":280,"height":62,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"8d5c171b5b1cea54","type":"text","text":"Finding an experimental collaborator and setting up everything might take too long for me to graduate in time.","x":1135,"y":-394,"width":280,"height":151,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"cfc0d8290fe027bd","type":"text","text":"We can simulate it by implementing an error correction cycle, QEC, consisting of encoding U, error process E, and recovery R.","x":1540,"y":129,"width":300,"height":151,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"dd8bc0602e29b3f8","type":"text","text":"In encoding U we do unitary operations to set the state of the 5 qubits to one of the logical qubit states.","x":1976,"y":129,"width":261,"height":151},
		{"id":"17af071ea23a664c","type":"text","text":"In the error process E the system goes through time-evolution, accumulating errors. These errors come from dissipation and decoherence, but in the leakage case also from transmon interaction.","x":1976,"y":360,"width":261,"height":245,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"69dce71e92dbf7b2","type":"text","text":"In the recovery R, I think we measure the qubits to find the errors?","x":1976,"y":680,"width":261,"height":100},
		{"id":"01732c1b9d17a64a","type":"text","text":"Our simulations would require special access, so it is difficult to say if this is possible.","x":1562,"y":-514,"width":257,"height":120,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"e10c1730ba91bcb7","type":"text","text":"We could maybe do a simulation of our LRU in a QC, so that 2 qubits would make a single qubit with states |0>, |1>, |2> and |3>. Setting this up is a lot of work!","x":1562,"y":-290,"width":257,"height":209,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"ce3710435da8865e","type":"text","text":"Contact someone and just ask!","x":1978,"y":-536,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"c73a02d4e5fd068f","type":"text","text":"IQM with their Helmi 5 qubit QC would be perfect for us.","x":1978,"y":-417,"width":253,"height":98,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"e32d433c7327e590","type":"text","text":"At first, our error process could just consist of transmon dynamics as normal, with dissipation and decoherence. We would **not** include the LRU yet.","x":2440,"y":382,"width":280,"height":200,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"80a38a76f5763b4a","type":"text","text":"We can add LRU to see if it improves the setup.","x":3060,"y":452,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"03558357165db9d9","type":"text","text":"Simulating 5 qubit code with LRU can be a numerical challenge.","x":2795,"y":780,"width":265,"height":95,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"0935d84bdc52fc0f","type":"text","text":"If needed we could add driving to simulate gate operations, which will also cause leakage.","x":2795,"y":987,"width":241,"height":135},
		{"id":"79549cdbddf831b3","type":"text","text":"We could derive an effective model for the transmon connected to the LRU, with this 5 qubit code and also 7 qubit code should be possible!","x":3295,"y":780,"width":250,"height":183,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"e78e218d217bd882","type":"text","text":"We could do partial LRU, so that not every qubit of the code has its own LRU.","x":3295,"y":1183,"width":268,"height":105},
		{"id":"c75a7a56fcc940c8","type":"text","text":"We could do 2 transmon LRU instead of 3, it still might be nice enough.","x":3295,"y":1023,"width":247,"height":105},
		{"id":"bbceee4a8a95f991","type":"text","text":"It still might possible to do.","x":3295,"y":1343,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"3a7d60419aabc390","type":"text","text":"We can split the model into two parts. One consists of the qubit dynamics, other of the effective stack dynamics.","x":3700,"y":787,"width":260,"height":169,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"1b5d8da65b5cf2c0","type":"text","text":"Diagonalisize Hamiltonian in terms of annihilation operators. In both cases the Hamiltonian is tri-diagonal, which should be easy to diagonalisize.","x":4140,"y":780,"width":280,"height":178,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ce407ea5ab1b879a","type":"text","text":"Combine qubit and stack dynamics to one effective model.","x":4900,"y":822,"width":266,"height":94,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"196e402ea79fa336","type":"text","text":"From diagonalization you get unitary U, with that you get dressed oberators b = Ua. Express master equation in these operators, trace out b_2 and b_3, and simulate in this basis.","x":4540,"y":780,"width":260,"height":241,"color":"6"}
	],
